% new: repository read at the source on 18 Nov 2026 at commit b2a61c46c157 (full hash
% b2a61c46c157860b57faa163341fda725c629139), the commit pinned by Tan--Zhang ref. [11]. README states irrationality of
% Li2(1/k), k >= 2, and Li2(-1/k), k >= 1; of Li2(+-2/k), Li2(+-3/k), Li2(+-4/k) beyond explicit thresholds
% (2/k: k >= 13, -2/k: k >= 16; 3/k: 56, 62; 4/k: 183, 194); of Li2(+-p/q) for p >= 5 and q >= 0.1851 p^(84/17)
% (shifted for the negative sign); a threshold table for p = 5..20, 25, 50, 100, 1000. No irrationality measure is
% stated. Main theorem Li2RationalAcceptance.originalStatement (lean/RationalCheck.lean); Apache-2.0. Author name
% from Tan--Zhang ref. [11]. Arithmetic rate (8/3)log q - (9/4)log(q - eps p) - 6 log p + 72/25 as quoted in
% Tan--Zhang (2.2), local text line 157 (constant 72/25 confirmed from the PDF).
